&lt;li&gt;Being passionate about our mission and our customers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Accounting &amp;amp; Reporting Manager, you will ensure accurate, timely and IFRS-compliant accounting and reporting as Catawiki continues to grow. You will strengthen the finance function through effective controls, scalable processes and a clear understanding of the story behind the figures.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will lead and develop the Accounting &amp;amp; Reporting team, partner with stakeholders across the organisation and ensure the financial implications of new business initiatives are appropriately captured and accounted for.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the month-end close to ensure accurate, timely and IFRS-compliant accounting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver timely monthly, quarterly and annual reporting, translating financial results into clear presentations for the Management Team, Executive Board and investors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure compliance with national and local legal, accounting and regulatory requirements, keeping track of existing and emerging legislation and policies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage relationships with local accountants and external auditors to ensure compliance with local regulations and appropriate accounting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve financial processes, reporting systems and internal controls to support efficient, accurate and timely reporting as the organisation grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with internal stakeholders on cross-functional projects, ensuring the financial implications of new business initiatives are captured and appropriately accounted for.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop the Accounting &amp;amp; Reporting team, building its capabilities in a continuously changing environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An academic degree in accounting and an RA, CPA or equivalent qualification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 8 years of successful experience in financial control and accounting within an international company and/or a Big Four accountancy firm.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of IFRS and the ability to apply it to accounting and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong leadership skills, with experience developing teams and strengthening the finance function in a changing environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English, with the ability to communicate effectively with teams, management and other stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A hands-on and flexible working style, with the ability to move between pragmatic execution and conceptual thinking while managing multiple projects and priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical proficiency and proven ability to use automation and AI tools to improve efficiency and drive innovation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How We Work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with stakeholders within Finance and across teams such as HR and Tech on initiatives with cross-functional impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We take ownership and work independently while continuing to build and develop a high-performing team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We adapt to evolving responsibilities as the organisation grows, taking on additional projects and priorities when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We Combine hands-on execution with broader conceptual thinking to continuously improve finance processes and ways of working.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
