&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;The software and systems you work on directly protect personnel and defend European and national sovereignty.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;You will work alongside industry-leading minds on autonomous systems, advanced propulsion, and secure cyber platforms.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;We foster a fast-paced, collaborative environment where bold ideas are supported by serious R&amp;amp;D backing.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;STARK is a European defence technology company building the next generation of unmanned systems. Rapid scaling requires precision engineering and reproducible manufacturing that never compromise on mission reliability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline; font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You own the structural, kinematic, and aerodynamic packaging architecture of the Gambit airframe — including carbon-composite primary structures, high-reliability folding mechanisms, and payload bays.&lt;br&gt;You aren&#39;t just designing mechanical components; you are architecting a rugged, lightweight tactical airframe that survives heavy field handling and aerodynamic loads while remaining simple to mass-produce.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline; font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead mechanical design of airframe structures, wing folding mechanisms, quick-release arms, and internal structural chassis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform FEA (structural, modal, thermal) and mass-property optimizations to meet stringent strength-to-weight targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish GD&amp;amp;T standards, tolerance stack-up analyses, and mechanical interface control documents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive Design for Manufacture (DFM) for carbon-fiber composites, CNC machined aluminum, injection-molded plastics, and 3D printing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead structural qualification tests (static load, drop testing, vibration per MIL-STD-810H).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor mechanical engineers through CAD reviews and prototyping iterations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline; font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5–8 years in aerospace mechanical design, UAV structures, lightweight robotics, or precision mechanisms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience bringing mechanical systems from clean-sheet CAD through tooling and flight qualification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced proficiency in parametric 3D CAD (SolidWorks, CATIA).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in composite design/manufacturing (prepreg, wet layup, bladder molding, sandwich panels).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in FEA tools (Ansys, Nastran, or SolidWorks Simulation) and GD&amp;amp;T per ASME Y14.5 / ISO 1101.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional working proficiency in English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be a citizen of a NATO member state (due to export control and security regulations).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
