&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we are looking for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Principal Combat Designer you will be responsible for creating and improving the combat mechanics for our diverse characters to make our game more fun, challenging and engaging.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we will do together:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with Design Director, and other Design Leads to drive and execute the vision for combat design for a robust online multiplayer experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and craft expert-level player combat mechanics, weapons and abilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate with Leads and Directors of other disciplines, particularly art and engineering, and ensure that everyone is on the same page before beginning mechanics/feature development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advocate for the player, always putting the player experience first when considering and making all design decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A can-do attitude that is player oriented…mechanics design is one of the most hotly debated areas of design, but you remember that simplicity is often a player’s best friend.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least two shipped AAA titles where you worked in mechanics design capacity&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert knowledge of off-the-shelf design tools, and expertise with Unreal Engine (UE5 preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep professional understanding of the many major mechanics and gameplay features found in contemporary game titles, and a keen knowledge for how those mechanics and features work.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong creative and technical problem-solving skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
