&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Verve has created a more efficient and privacy-focused way to buy and monetize advertising. Verve is an ecosystem of demand and supply technologies fusing data, media, and technology together to deliver results and growth to both advertisers and publishers–no matter the screen or location, no matter who, what, or where a customer is. With 30 offices across the globe and with an eye on servicing forward-thinking advertising customers, Verve’s solutions are trusted by more than 90 of the United States’ top 100 advertisers, 4,000 publishers globally, and the world’s top demand-side platforms. Learn more at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://verve.com/&quot;&gt;verve.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About Verve Retail Media&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;The biggest challenge for advertisers in physical retail is the lack of measurable proof of effectiveness. Brands invest millions in advertising at the point of sale, but they cannot demonstrate whether those investments actually generated purchases.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Verve Retail Media (VRM) solves this problem. We market and operate digital advertising screens across several thousand grocery, drugstore and convenience store locations, connecting them with digital coupons and retargeting campaigns on connected TV (CTV) and other offsite channels.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Brands don’t book isolated advertising formats; instead, they book 360-degree campaigns that start at home and continue all the way through to an in-store purchase. This enables closed-loop measurement based on actual point-of-sale transaction data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;VRM is the independent retail media division of publicly listed Verve Group SE. We operate like a rapidly scaling startup, with an AI-first strategy across all functions. We also have access to the infrastructure of an international ad tech company that delivers more than one trillion advertising impressions per year.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI needs data. While the digital world has been mapped, the vast, untapped data of human behavior and location intelligence remains the greatest challenge and the greatest opportunity. We are creating a robust data platform and sophisticated geo-targeting infrastructure that enables brands to understand shopper behavior and reach audiences effectively outside the physical store.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In order to build this platform, we are looking for a visionary Technical Product Manager to lead the development of our cutting-edge capabilities. In this role, you will sit at the intersection of AdTech, Location Data, and AI, building the infrastructure that allows brands and retailers to engage shoppers through off-site media and precise geographic targeting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own the roadmap for our core data platform, advanced geo-targeting tools, and off-site ad integrations. &lt;strong&gt;Crucially, you will own the entire product lifecycle from initial discovery and scoping all the way through to commercial readiness. This end-to-end ownership requires tight collaboration with our Sales and Operations teams to ensure what we build is not only technically sound but also highly marketable and operationally scalable.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A critical focus of this role will be building products that scale globally, with a specific emphasis on spearheading our rollout and expansion into the US market. Your goal is to turn complex location and behavioral data into intelligent, monetizable media channels that drive measurable results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join a collaborative team of PMs dedicated to the holistic success of our Retail Media Platform. You won&#39;t build in a silo; you&#39;ll ensure a cohesive, unified roadmap across our data infrastructure and off-site touchpoints, driving a revolution in retail technology on a global scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;Product Strategy, Lifecycle Ownership &amp;amp; Global Roadmap&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end product development process from discovery and ideation to commercial launch and operational readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and execute the product roadmap for our data platform, geo-targeting tools, and off-site media capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spearhead product localization and scaling efforts for international expansion, with a primary focus on the US market rollout. Ensure compliance with regional data privacy regulations (e.g., CCPA, GDPR).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate business goals into technical specifications, working closely with Sales to validate market fit and with Operations to ensure seamless delivery and support post-launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Platform &amp;amp; Geo-Targeting Development&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect the logic and infrastructure for our advanced geo-targeting tool, enabling precise audience segmentation based on location intelligence and behavioral data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the development of robust data pipelines capable of processing and analyzing vast amounts of location and transaction data securely and efficiently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop features for closed-loop campaign measurement and attribution, linking off-site ad exposure to online or offline transaction data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AdTech &amp;amp; Off-Site Integrations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead integrations with external AdTech partners, including Supply Side Platforms (SSPs), Demand Side Platforms (DSPs), and Data Management Platforms (DMPs) to facilitate seamless off-site ad delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure compliance with industry standards (e.g., OpenRTB, VAST) while adapting them for specialized location-based and off-site media environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration &amp;amp; Market Expansion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner intimately with Sales to understand client needs and define Go-To-Market strategies for new features, ensuring commercial viability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Operations to build scalable processes for onboarding, campaign execution, and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the primary technical liaison between our engineering team and external partners/brands, especially during international rollouts, translating complex constraints into clear value propositions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Ideal Candidate&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must-Haves:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Fluency:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong understanding of APIs, cloud architecture, and large-scale data pipelines. You are comfortable discussing JSON payloads one minute and global business strategy the next.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;End-to-End Ownership:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven track record of taking products from 0 to 1, managing the entire lifecycle from discovery to commercial rollout.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data &amp;amp; AdTech Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven experience building data products, audience targeting tools, or working extensively within the AdTech ecosystem (DSPs, DMPs, SSPs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expansion Mindset:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience or strong interest in scaling products internationally; an understanding of the nuances and privacy landscapes of the US market is highly desirable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data-Driven:&lt;/strong&gt; Ability to define success metrics (Match Rates, CPM, ROAS, Incrementality) and use data to prioritize features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice-to-Haves:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with location intelligence or geospatial data analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in retail media networks or off-site retail media strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with clean room technologies or advanced attribution modeling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Domain specific expertise is a plus but we will onboard you in case you don’t have it:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience as a Product Manager or Technical Product Manager, with a specific focus on AdTech, MarTech, or Data Platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Retail Media Knowledge:&lt;/strong&gt; Understanding of the Retail Media landscape, specifically how off-site media budgets are allocated and measured.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why You&#39;ll Enjoy Working Here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role isn’t for everyone - and that’s intentional. We’re building Verve Retail Media from the ground up, reducing legacy structures, places to hide, and “passenger seats”. This is a place for people who want to build, take ownership, and see the direct impact of their work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You won’t be one of many - you’ll be one of the few shaping how this company grows, decides, and wins. And every role counts - from Office Management to Chief of Staff to this role.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re looking for comfort, predictability, or perfectly defined lanes, this probably isn’t your environment. If you’re looking for steep growth, real responsibility, and the chance to work with people who raise your bar - you’ll feel at home here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What you can expect:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Real ownership from day one - take decisions, not just tasks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A steep learning curve - accelerated growth through real responsibility, not theory&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High-performing peers - work with ambitious, driven people who challenge and support you&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct impact - your work will shape products, processes, and outcomes in real time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cutting-edge tools - including AI-powered workflows that multiply your output&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuous development - training budget, internal learning formats, and language courses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a place where expectations are high - and so is the opportunity to grow, contribute, and build something meaningful.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Verve provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;Verve provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If you are a California resident subject to the California Consumer Privacy Act, &lt;a href=&quot;https://verve.com/california-applicant-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;click here&lt;/a&gt; to understand how Verve processes your personal information and how you can exercise your rights.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;If you are located in the EU or UK visit our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot; href=&quot;https://verve.com/applicant-privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;privacy policy&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt; to understand how Verve processes your personal information and how you can exercise your rights.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Twilio, we’re shaping the future of communications, all from the comfort of our homes. We deliver innovative solutions to&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://customers.twilio.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://customers.twilio.com/&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;hundreds of thousands of businesses&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;and empower millions of developers worldwide to craft personalized customer experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our dedication to &lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.twilio.com/en-us/blog/open-work&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.twilio.com/en-us/blog/open-work&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;remote-first work&lt;/a&gt;, and strong culture of connection and global inclusion means that no matter your location, you’re part of a vibrant team with diverse experiences making a global impact each day. As we continue to revolutionize how the world interacts, we’re acquiring new skills and experiences that make work feel truly rewarding. Your career at Twilio is in your hands.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hiring and how we work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We use Artificial Intelligence (AI) to help make our hiring process efficient. That said, every hiring decision is made by real Twilions!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Also, while we are a remote-first company, you may be asked to report in person on an ad-hoc basis for team gatherings, functional off-sites or customer meetings.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;See yourself at Twilio&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join the team as Twilio’s next Strategic Account Executive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is needed to sell into high value prospects and customers. This person will play a key role in further growing the business across EMEA with a particular focus on Northern Europe. The candidate will be responsible for managing fast growing customers in the region. Focused mainly on Product cross and up-sell and revenue growth, as well as sourcing net new opportunities within a set of accounts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you’ll:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Servicing the fastest growing customers in the region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growing our revenue and share of wallet within your key account list.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opening doors to the purchase of Twilio’s products and services - including voice, messaging, email, contact centre, account security software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintaining the highest levels of customer satisfaction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create pricing proposals, negotiating terms and managing the contract process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Selling solutions to a technical and business audience.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building trust and mutual respect with technical customers and peers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thinking outside of the box and having extraordinary interpersonal and communication skills to make complex contractual, technical, and financial details sound simple.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balancing challenging priorities and handling multiple projects/deals at the same time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Twilio values diverse experiences from all kinds of industries, and we encourage everyone who meets the required qualifications to apply. If your career is just starting or hasn&#39;t followed a traditional path, don&#39;t let that stop you from considering Twilio. We are always looking for people who will bring something new to the table!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;*Required:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of Account Management/Sales experience covering selling and closing complex technical solutions to a large customer base.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;History of working with accounts ranging from large multinational enterprise customers to Digital Natives.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and maintaining relationships up to C-suite.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success by achieving quota on a consistent basis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of Account Management experience and a solid understanding of how to cross and upsell solutions within a mature customer base.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A solid understanding of financial reporting within a direct customer base - Revenue tracking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling both to a business and technical stakeholders.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience and understanding of working in the communications market is preferable.&amp;nbsp; Have sold or worked with Messaging, Voice, Email, Contact Centre, Account Security Verification.&amp;nbsp; Or have prior experience in a traditional telecommunications environment/business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curious networker&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The position will be remote and based in the United Kingdom or Ireland.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We prioritize connection and opportunities to build relationships with our customers and each other. For this role, approximately 25%&amp;nbsp; travel is anticipated to help you connect in-person in a meaningful way.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working at Twilio offers many benefits, including competitive pay, generous time off, ample parental and wellness leave, healthcare, a retirement savings program, and much more. Offerings vary by location.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Twilio thinks big. Do you?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We like to solve problems, take initiative, pitch in when needed, and are always up for trying new things. That&#39;s why we seek out colleagues who embody our values — something we call &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.twilio.com/company/values&quot;&gt;Twilio Magic&lt;/a&gt;. Additionally, we empower employees to build &lt;a href=&quot;https://twilio.org/support-and-resources/impact-fund&quot;&gt;positive change in their communities&lt;/a&gt; by supporting their volunteering and donation efforts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;So, if you&#39;re ready to unleash your full potential, do your best work, and be the best version of yourself, apply now! If this role isn&#39;t what you&#39;re looking for, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.twilio.com/company/jobs#open-positions&quot;&gt;please consider other open positions.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stay alert to recruitment fraud&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We care about your safety. Scammers sometimes impersonate Twilio recruiters through fake job postings, emails, websites, or messages. Please ensure you are engaging with an official @&lt;a href=&quot;http://twilio.com&quot;&gt;twilio.com&lt;/a&gt; email address. We will never ask for payment, gift cards, cryptocurrency, or banking information during the recruiting process. We do not make job offers without a formal interview process or conduct interviews exclusively through text-based messaging apps.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Twilio is proud to be an equal opportunity employer.&lt;/strong&gt; We do not discriminate based upon race, religion, color, national origin, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, reproductive health decisions, or related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, status as a protected veteran, status as an individual with a disability, genetic information, political views or activity, or other applicable legally protected characteristics. We also consider qualified applicants with criminal histories, consistent with applicable federal, state and local law. Qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records will be considered for employment in accordance with the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for Employers and the California Fair Chance Act. Additionally, Twilio participates in the E-Verify program in certain locations, as required by law.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Liftoff&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; is a leading AI-powered performance marketing platform for the mobile app economy. Our end-to-end technology stack helps app marketers acquire and retain high-value users, while enabling publishers to maximize revenue across programmatic and direct demand.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Liftoff’s solutions, including Accelerate, Direct, Monetize, Intelligence, and Vungle Exchange, support over 6,600 mobile businesses across 74 countries in sectors such as gaming, social, finance, ecommerce, and entertainment. Founded in 2012 and headquartered in Redwood City, CA, Liftoff has a diverse, global presence.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About this team:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Liftoff, the View Master team plays a crucial role in the company&#39;s success. Our team builds mobile SDKs (iOS, Android, Windows), and systems that connect Liftoff’s publishers with advertisers, managing applications, campaigns, and creatives that feed into our ad serving pipeline. We create innovative advertisements viewed by millions daily, ensuring a seamless user experience and optimizing ad performance.&amp;nbsp; We&#39;re a group of innovative engineers who leverage the latest technology to develop efficient and scalable systems. If you&#39;re passionate about building and scaling low-latency, high-throughput systems, we&#39;d be delighted to speak with you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the technical direction for new ad format development in the SDK, driving decisions on native/web architecture and cross-platform compatibility without needing detailed direction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently scope and lead ambiguous, cross-team initiatives from problem definition through rollout — e.g., overhauling automation quality and creative/SDK interoperability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive multi-quarter improvements to system efficiency, reliability, and rendering performance, owning tradeoffs between short- and long-term solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set and evangelize testing strategy and standards (unit, integration, automated) across the team, not just execute against existing practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and drive experimentation and canary-release strategy for ad unit performance, including recommending which approaches to pursue&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technically lead and mentor other engineers on the team, including guiding junior/mid-level engineers&#39; project work and growth (not just informal mentorship)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the team in cross-functional and roadmap discussions, influencing prioritization and scope rather than only attending for alignment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uphold and help define the team&#39;s engineering bar for code quality, security/privacy, cost efficiency, and production hygiene (oncall, monitoring, documentation)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to hiring and leveling: participate in interviews, help hold the technical bar for the role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science or related fields and 6 years of relevant experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in JavaScript (ES6+), CSS preprocessors, and HTML5, with demonstrated ability to make architectural decisions in this stack&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in and helping shape Agile processes for a team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills, including the ability to influence technical direction across engineering and product without formal authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous AdTech experience is highly valued&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing mobile applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced automated testing strategies using tools such as AWS Device Farm, iOS and Android simulators, Playwright, Selenium, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;This role is eligible for remote or hybrid work out of our London office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel Expectations:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;We offer several opportunities for in-person team gatherings, including but not limited to project meetings, regional meet-ups, and company-wide events. We expect our employees to attend these gatherings at least once per quarter. These gatherings provide essential opportunities for collaboration, communication, and team building.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Liftoff offers all employees a full compensation package that includes equity and health/vision/dental benefits associated with your country of residence. Base compensation will vary based on the candidate&#39;s location and experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-REMOTE&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-NM1&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Liftoff offers a fast-paced, collaborative, and innovative work environment where employees are empowered to grow and make an impact. We’re shaping the future of the mobile app ecosystem—join us and help accelerate what’s next.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Liftoff’s compensation strategy includes competitive salaries, equity, and benefits designed to support employee well-being and performance. We benchmark compensation based on role, level, and location to ensure fairness and market alignment. Benefits may include medical coverage, wellness stipends, and additional perks based on your country of residence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Liftoff is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees and applicants regardless of race, ethnicity, national origin, age, marital status, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agency and Third Party Recruiter Notice:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Liftoff does not accept unsolicited resumes from individual recruiters or third-party recruiting agencies in response to job postings. No fee will be paid to third parties who submit unsolicited candidates directly to our hiring managers or Recruiting Team. All candidates must be submitted via our Applicant Tracking System by approved Liftoff vendors who have been expressly requested to make a submission by our Recruiting Team for a specific job opening. No placement fees will be paid to any firm unless such a request has been made by the Liftoff Recruiting Team and such a candidate was submitted to the Liftoff Recruiting Team via our Applicant Tracking System.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Liftoff&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; is a leading AI-powered performance marketing platform for the mobile app economy. Our end-to-end technology stack helps app marketers acquire and retain high-value users, while enabling publishers to maximize revenue across programmatic and direct demand.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Liftoff’s solutions, including Accelerate, Direct, Monetize, Intelligence, and Vungle Exchange, support over 6,600 mobile businesses across 74 countries in sectors such as gaming, social, finance, ecommerce, and entertainment. Founded in 2012 and headquartered in Redwood City, CA, Liftoff has a diverse, global presence.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Senior Account Manager, you&#39;ll be a senior individual contributor and a cornerstone of our commercial team. You&#39;ll own an above-average revenue target and be expected to consistently deliver, and exceed, it. Operating with a high degree of autonomy; you&#39;ll manage complex, high-value deals end-to-end, drive forecast accuracy, and actively shape how we go to market. This role sits at the intersection of sales execution, cross-functional collaboration, and strategic influence: you&#39;ll be as comfortable building a Looker report as you are leading a high-stakes negotiation, and as effective with Finance and Product as you are in front of a customer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and grow a portfolio of key accounts, consistently exceeding revenue targets and carrying above-average quota.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate pipeline and revenue forecasts, surfacing risks proactively and identifying in-quarter opportunities to accelerate attainment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead complex, high-value negotiations; adapting style to different stakeholders and closing with minimal concessions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and tailor compelling value propositions, running multi-channel outreach to fill and advance pipeline efficiently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage multiple concurrent work-streams with clear ownership, balancing scope, time, and quality with minimal oversight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally with Product, Marketing, Finance, and Operations to deliver solutions and influence roadmap priorities based on customer feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyse multi-dimensional data in Looker, AI and Google Sheets to surface actionable insights and build compelling, decision-driving narratives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach junior team members and contribute to a culture of proactive, well-received feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of exceeding revenue targets in digital advertising, account management, or consultative sales; preferably within mobile or programmatic ad-tech.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong forecasting discipline and pipeline management skills, with experience running high-value deals from prospecting through close.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled negotiator who adapts approach intuitively and is comfortable managing complex, multi-stakeholder sales cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in Looker, AI and Google Sheets, with the ability to analyse complex data sets and build clear, impactful visualisations independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent cross-functional collaborator, with experience engaging Product, Finance, and Marketing beyond immediate deal needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High emotional intelligence, strong communication skills, and the ability to give and receive feedback constructively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree; advanced degree a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel up to 10% for client meetings and industry events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel Expectations:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We offer several opportunities for in-person team gatherings, including but not limited to project meetings, regional meetups, and company-wide events. We expect our employees to attend these gatherings at least once per quarter. These gatherings provide essential opportunities for collaboration, communication, and team building.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Liftoff offers all employees a full compensation package that includes equity and health/vision/dental benefits associated with your country of residence. Base compensation will vary based on the candidate&#39;s location and experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c-mrkdwn__highlight&quot;&gt;#LI-NM&lt;/span&gt;1&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-REMOTE&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Liftoff offers a fast-paced, collaborative, and innovative work environment where employees are empowered to grow and make an impact. We’re shaping the future of the mobile app ecosystem—join us and help accelerate what’s next.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Liftoff’s compensation strategy includes competitive salaries, equity, and benefits designed to support employee well-being and performance. We benchmark compensation based on role, level, and location to ensure fairness and market alignment. Benefits may include medical coverage, wellness stipends, and additional perks based on your country of residence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Liftoff is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees and applicants regardless of race, ethnicity, national origin, age, marital status, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agency and Third Party Recruiter Notice:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Liftoff does not accept unsolicited resumes from individual recruiters or third-party recruiting agencies in response to job postings. No fee will be paid to third parties who submit unsolicited candidates directly to our hiring managers or Recruiting Team. All candidates must be submitted via our Applicant Tracking System by approved Liftoff vendors who have been expressly requested to make a submission by our Recruiting Team for a specific job opening. No placement fees will be paid to any firm unless such a request has been made by the Liftoff Recruiting Team and such a candidate was submitted to the Liftoff Recruiting Team via our Applicant Tracking System.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Liftoff&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; is a leading AI-powered performance marketing platform for the mobile app economy. Our end-to-end technology stack helps app marketers acquire and retain high-value users, while enabling publishers to maximize revenue across programmatic and direct demand.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Liftoff’s solutions, including Accelerate, Direct, Monetize, Intelligence, and Vungle Exchange, support over 6,600 mobile businesses across 74 countries in sectors such as gaming, social, finance, ecommerce, and entertainment. Founded in 2012 and headquartered in Redwood City, CA, Liftoff has a diverse, global presence.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Liftoff is looking for a Commercial Legal Counsel that will assist the in-house legal department with Insertion Orders (Agreements), third party contracts and other legal needs. This position will support the Commercial, Finance and Accounting teams, located around the world.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;As a Commercial Legal Counsel at Liftoff, you will play a pivotal role in ensuring the seamless execution of contracts that drive our business forward. You will be at the intersection of legal expertise, meticulous organization, and collaborative teamwork. Your responsibilities will encompass contract drafting, negotiation, process improvement and training. As an essential part of our team, you&#39;ll contribute to the foundation of our business relationships and help us navigate the complex world of contracts with precision and efficiency. If you&#39;re passionate about detail-oriented work, contract law, and making a meaningful impact, this role is your opportunity to shine. Join us in shaping the way we manage contracts and elevate our commitment to excellence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft, review, and negotiate a wide range of contracts, including vendor agreements, customer contracts, and licensing agreements, to ensure compliance with company policies and legal requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with internal teams, including legal, sales/commercial, product, engineering, finance and accounting to understand contract terms, resolve issues, and provide guidance on contractual matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain an organized and up-to-date contract ticketing system, respond to each contract ticket in a timely manner and track contract milestones and deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in&amp;nbsp; contract compliance, addressing any deviations or breaches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in the development and improvement of contract templates and standard clauses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the contract approval process, ensuring proper authorization and documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide guidance and training to employees on contract-related matters and best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay updated on relevant laws and regulations impacting contract management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5-10 Years of experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Law, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience as a Contracts Counsel/Legal Counsel or in a similar role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of contract law and legal terminology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detail-oriented with exceptional organizational and time management abilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in contract management software or tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work collaboratively in a cross-functional team environment globally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in ad-tech is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is based in London or remotely within the United Kingdom, occasionally going into the office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is a contract position with the potential to become a full-time employee. The expected hours of work required for this position are 35 to 40 hours per week, with occasional early evening hours for team meetings, as the manager is located in our Redwood City office in California.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
