As a Paid Media Intern, you will be part of the digital marketing and e-commerce teams, collaborating closely with the Paid Media Specialist. Your role involves supporting and optimizing advertising activities across various channels, including PPC, paid social, display and affiliates. The internship offers a dynamic learning experience, providing hands-on exposure to the intricacies of paid media within fashion. You will be working daily with internal stakeholders and external partners such as Google, Meta and TikTok.&nbsp;Key Responsibilities:
Assist the Paid Media Specialist in the planning, execution and optimization of paid media campaigns
Work closely with the media agencies to support with the coordination and implementation of paid media plans
Assist in maintaining a content calendar for paid media campaigns, ensuring timely execution and alignment with overall marketing initiatives
Reviewing and testing of ads to ensure they align with the brand’s messaging, visual standards and campaign objective
Monitor and analyze campaign performance through internal dashboards and Google Analytics, providing insights to enhance the paid media strategy
Support in trade reporting and prepare weekly presentations
Collaborate with internal teams such as merchandising, buying, social media and retail marketing to ensure close alignment
Collaborate with external partners such as Google, TikTok and Snapchat to stay up to date on platform updates and new features.
Work closely with the creative team and support in briefing, and reviewing creative content and copy
Coordinate and save all paid media content in online folders
Assist in liaising with the translation agency to ensure advertising materials are accurately translated and relevant for international markets
Support in monitoring spend against budget and provide administrative support
Support with monthly validations of sales&nbsp;&nbsp;
Create benchmarks and perform competitor analysis&nbsp;
