Need to be enrolled in an accredited Bachelor/Master program during the entire internship period&nbsp;
Keen knowledge and interest in digital marketing and data analyzation&nbsp;
Experience with premium brands or the luxury sector is preferable but not a must&nbsp;
Previous marketing or e-com internship preferred&nbsp;
Experience and proficiency in MS Office software suites and preferably also in Google Analytics&nbsp;&nbsp;
Language: fluent in English, both verbal and written. Knowledge of an additional language (one that is served on KARL.com) is a nice advantage.
Profile: 
Curious, analytical with an eye for detail&nbsp;
Able to prioritize and multitask&nbsp;
Able to work independently as well as in a team&nbsp;
Interested and passionate about the fashion industry and cross-channel digital marketing&nbsp;
Flexible and adaptable, with a positive attitude&nbsp;
Able to work in a fast-paced and high-pressure environment&nbsp;
 Available for 6 months / 40 hours a week
