Caseware is one of Canada's original Fintech companies, having led the global audit and accounting software industry for over 30 years, with more than 500,000 users across 130 countries and available in 16 different languages. While you might not have heard of us (yet) over 36,000 accounting and audit professionals list Caseware as a skill on their LinkedIn profiles!As an&nbsp;Account&nbsp;Executive&nbsp;at&nbsp;Caseware, you play&nbsp;a central role&nbsp;in driving revenue growth. You expand our presence in the market, win new&nbsp;customers&nbsp;and strengthen relationships with existing ones. With strong closing skills and a sharp eye for new opportunities within your portfolio, you help build sustainable revenue and long-term partnerships. You also increase&nbsp;Caseware’s&nbsp;visibility by building a relevant network and positioning our solutions confidently in the market. Your work has a direct impact on customer loyalty, market&nbsp;position&nbsp;and the long-term success of the company.What you will be doing:
Drive active sales of&nbsp;Caseware’s&nbsp;solutions through consultative conversations, product&nbsp;presentations&nbsp;and confident management of the full sales cycle, working closely with Marketing, Consulting and Product Management.&nbsp;
Build and expand long-term customer relationships based on a clear understanding of individual needs, strengthening satisfaction,&nbsp;loyalty&nbsp;and future growth opportunities.&nbsp;
Increase market share and ARR within your territory by winning new customers, securing reliable deal&nbsp;outcomes&nbsp;and expanding existing accounts through upsell and cross-sell.&nbsp;
Develop and execute strategic sales and account plans, using cross-functional resources to unlock revenue potential and move opportunities to a successful close.&nbsp;
Manage your pipeline with discipline and deliver&nbsp;accurate&nbsp;forecasts that support clear decision-making and consistent progress toward sales targets.&nbsp;
Strengthen&nbsp;Caseware’s&nbsp;market presence and expand your professional network through active engagement with key decision-makers and relevant industry stakeholders.&nbsp;
Maintain complete and&nbsp;accurate&nbsp;documentation of all sales activities,&nbsp;data&nbsp;and contract details in the CRM to ensure transparency and efficient operations.&nbsp;
What you will bring:
5+ years of experience in enterprise technology or complex solution sales across large customer accounts&nbsp;
Solid understanding of the Software as a Service (SaaS) business model&nbsp;
Proven success in winning new customers and expanding existing enterprise accounts&nbsp;
Demonstrated ability to sell and navigate complex enterprise organizations&nbsp;
Experience&nbsp;demonstrating&nbsp;complex software applications to customers&nbsp;
Strong business acumen with the ability to understand complex business challenges&nbsp;
Executive presence with the ability to communicate effectively with senior leadership&nbsp;
Ability to&nbsp;identify&nbsp;influencers and decision-makers and manage stakeholder dynamics throughout the sales cycle&nbsp;
Ability to manage multiple complex sales cycles simultaneously&nbsp;
Strong negotiation skills with a focus on&nbsp;maintaining&nbsp;commercial value&nbsp;
Consistent&nbsp;track record&nbsp;of achieving or exceeding sales quota targets&nbsp;
Confident communication skills that help build trust quickly with key stakeholders&nbsp;
Structured and dependable working style that supports long-term customer partnerships&nbsp;
Strong commercial awareness and the ability to&nbsp;identify&nbsp;business opportunities and value drivers&nbsp;
Motivation, curiosity, and a practical, solution-focused approach to working with customers&nbsp;
Knowledge of audit, finance, or accounting is a plus&nbsp;
Strong Dutch and English communication skills, both written and spoken&nbsp;
Operate with an AI-first mindset,&nbsp;leveraging&nbsp;tools to enhance productivity, decision-making, and day-to-day work.&nbsp;
Champion a culture of AI experimentation — proactively explore, adopt, and share emerging tools relevant to your role.&nbsp;
What we offer:
Competitive base salary + very attractive commission model&nbsp;
25–30 vacation days&nbsp;
Hybrid / remote work options&nbsp;
Pension contribution&nbsp;
Learning and development budget&nbsp;
International team and growth opportunities&nbsp;
What's in it for you:▪️Innovation is at our core. We work with cutting-edge technology in accounting and financial reporting, constantly pushing the boundaries to create impactful software solutions.&nbsp;▪️We are committed to a collaborative culture, where your ideas are valued, and knowledge sharing is encouraged within a supportive, inclusive team.&nbsp;▪️Work-life balance is important to us. We offer flexible work options, remote opportunities, and generous time-off policies to ensure a healthy work-life balance.&nbsp;▪️We offer competitive compensation, including a competitive salary and comprehensive benefits such as health insurance and retirement plans.&nbsp;▪️We are driven by impactful work. Your contributions directly affect how our clients manage financial processes and drive their success.&nbsp;▪️Recognition and rewards matter to us. We celebrate hard work through recognition programs, performance bonuses, and opportunities for career growth.&nbsp;▪️We embrace global opportunities. Work on international projects and collaborate with a diverse, global team.&nbsp;About Caseware:Caseware's cutting-edge software products are meticulously designed for accounting firms, corporations, and governments.&nbsp;Our teams are continually collaborating, innovating, and building upon our existing suite of products. With a customer-focused mindset, we are building technology that is shaping what the future of audits, financial reporting, and financial data analytics will look like.With a recent strategic investment from Hg Capital in 2020, Caseware is now in its next major growth phase as we double down on the people and products that have made Caseware so successful to date.One of Caseware's core values is Many Voices, One Team and with that in mind, we're dedicated to building teams as diverse as our customers in an equitable and inclusive way. We welcome and encourage candidates of all backgrounds to apply. Should you require accommodations or have any questions at any point during the application or interview process, please e-mail our People Operations team at ----- style="font-size: 16px">AI Usage:The recruitment process may use AI assisted tools but not for candidate screening or assessment. All final hiring decisions are made by humans to ensure fairness, transparency, and oversight.&nbsp;Background Check:Any candidates successful in obtaining an offer for a position will need to successfully complete a background check through Certn.co which typically includes an Identity Verification and Criminal Record Check. Executives and Senior Managers will undergo a Soft Credit Check as well. Candidates residing&nbsp;in the Netherlands and Germany are excluded from undergoing background checks via Certn.co&nbsp;Security and Fraud:Caseware takes the security of candidates seriously. All legitimate communication from us will come from email addresses ending in ----- and our open positions are always listed on reputable job boards and on our website https://jobs.lever.co/caseware. We will NEVER ask for payment or financial information from you. If you receive an unsolicited job offer, proceed with extreme caution.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Find Jobs in Netherlands on Arbeitnow

TomTom's map is seen by millions of people every day in dashboards, on phones, and across partner products worldwide. As a&nbsp;Staff UX Designer&nbsp;on the Map&nbsp;Visualisation&nbsp;team, you will own the visual and technical direction of how our&nbsp;2D&nbsp;and 3D geospatial data comes to life in real time.&nbsp;


This is not a traditional UX role.&nbsp;You'll&nbsp;operate&nbsp;at the intersection of cartographic design, real-time rendering, and product engineering, partnering directly with software engineers to define, prototype, and ship features within TomTom's&nbsp;modern&nbsp;map&nbsp;rendering&nbsp;engine.&nbsp;


You'll&nbsp;report into the UX Design organisation but spend&nbsp;significant time&nbsp;embedded with engineering and product teams, influencing the roadmap, shaping architectural decisions, and ensuring that what we build is both technically sound and visually compelling.&nbsp;

What You'll Do 



Set the Visual Direction&nbsp;Define and evolve the long-term vision for TomTom's map rendering across 2D and 3D, from cartographic styling to photorealistic environments. Establish and&nbsp;maintain&nbsp;design principles that scale across product lines, platforms, and global markets.&nbsp;






Partner with Engineering on Rendering&nbsp;Features&nbsp;Work side-by-side with graphics and platform engineers to specify, develop, and&nbsp;validate&nbsp;new rendering capabilities in TomTom's&nbsp;Premium Map Display engine.&nbsp;Translate design intent into concrete renderer specifications,&nbsp;including lighting models,&nbsp;shader&nbsp;parameters, level-of-detail strategies, and style-layer behaviour. Participate actively in solution design reviews, pull requests, and sprint ceremonies.&nbsp;






Own Core Map Styles End-to-End&nbsp;Take map experiences from early ideation through prototyping, implementation, and production delivery. Enhance and&nbsp;maintain&nbsp;TomTom's core map styles, balancing aesthetic quality, readability, and runtime performance.&nbsp;






Drive Product and Roadmap Decisions&nbsp;Operate as a staff-level contributor who shapes what gets built and why. Make complex product trade-offs across visual fidelity,&nbsp;rendering&nbsp;performance, SDK compatibility, and data constraints. Influence the Map&nbsp;Visualisation&nbsp;roadmap in close collaboration with Product Management, Map Data, and Engineering leadership.&nbsp;






Inform Tooling and Workflows&nbsp;Define requirements for internal cartographic design tooling and authoring pipelines.&nbsp;Identify&nbsp;gaps in the current workflow and advocate for tooling investments that improve design velocity and quality.&nbsp;






Champion User and Customer Insight&nbsp;Participate in user research, customer success conversations, and competitive analysis to ground visual and technical decisions in real-world needs. Translate customer feedback into actionable design and&nbsp;rendering&nbsp;improvements.&nbsp;



What You'll Need 


Cartography &amp; Map Visualisation&nbsp;




Deep&nbsp;expertise&nbsp;in digital cartography, multi-zoom map design, and cartographic conventions across cultures and regions.&nbsp;






Proven&nbsp;track record&nbsp;of building advanced, visually compelling 2D and 3D map experiences,&nbsp;from&nbsp;lane-level detail to global overviews.&nbsp;






Extensive experience working with spatial datasets and geospatial data pipelines.&nbsp;




Real-Time Rendering &amp; Technical Craft&nbsp;




Strong understanding of real-time 3D rendering concepts:&nbsp;shaders, lighting,&nbsp;modeling, texturing,&nbsp;level-of-detail,&nbsp;post&nbsp;effects&nbsp;and&nbsp;runtime&nbsp;performance&nbsp;optimizations.&nbsp;






Demonstrated ability to work within and influence a rendering technology stack;&nbsp;experience with&nbsp;mapping libraries&nbsp;such as&nbsp;MapLibre,&nbsp;Mapbox&nbsp;GL&nbsp;JS,&nbsp;and game engines&nbsp;such as Unity.&nbsp;








Proficiency&nbsp;in&nbsp;handling a range of graphical styles: from&nbsp;photorealistic&nbsp;to&nbsp;stylised rendering of real-world environments.&nbsp;




Software Development Collaboration&nbsp;




Significant experience&nbsp;working inside product engineering teams, not&nbsp;adjacent to&nbsp;them. You understand agile methodologies, CI/CD workflows,&nbsp;git,&nbsp;pull request reviews, branching strategies, and feature-flag rollouts.&nbsp;






Ability to read and reason about code. Hands-on coding skills are a plus but not a prerequisite;&nbsp;what matters is that you can engage credibly with engineers on technical implementation details and architectural decisions.&nbsp;






Fluency with solution design documents, technical specifications, and cross-functional RFC processes.&nbsp;




Staff-Level Leadership&nbsp;




8+ years of relevant professional experience in UX design, technical art, cartographic design, or a closely related discipline.&nbsp;






Bachelor's or&nbsp;Master's&nbsp;degree in Cartography, Geography, GIS, Computer Science, UX Design, or a related field,&nbsp;or equivalent professional experience.&nbsp;






Demonstrated ability to drive alignment across engineering, product, and design without direct authority.&nbsp;






Track record&nbsp;of influencing technical and product roadmaps at an organisational level.&nbsp;






Strong documentation, storytelling, and presentation skills. You can make a renderer specification as clear as a design critique.&nbsp;




Mindset&nbsp;&amp; Working Style&nbsp;




Deep user empathy paired with pragmatic product thinking.&nbsp;






Comfort navigating ambiguity in complex, multi-layered technology stacks.&nbsp;






Collaborative and&nbsp;low ego. You build trust with engineers, PMs,&nbsp;marketeers,&nbsp;designers&nbsp;and customers.&nbsp;






High attention to detail with a passion for craft at every zoom level.&nbsp;




Nice to Have 




Hands-on&nbsp;proficiency&nbsp;in front-end development (JavaScript,&nbsp;WebGL,&nbsp;etc).&nbsp;






Experience in the automotive, fleet management, or&nbsp;logistics&nbsp;industries.&nbsp;






Familiarity with consumer location-technology products and emerging trends in spatial computing, AR navigation, or digital twins.&nbsp;








Experience defining or contributing to design systems at scale.&nbsp;




What we offer A competitive compensation package, of course. &nbsp;Time and resources to grow and develop, including a personal development budget and paid leave for learning days, as well as paid access to e-learning resources such as O’Reilly and LinkedIn Learning.&nbsp;Time to support life outside of work, with enhanced parental leave plus paid leave to care for loved ones and volunteer in local communities.&nbsp;&nbsp;Work flexibility, where TomTom’ers, in agreement with their manager and team, use both the office and home to focus, collaborate, learn and socialize. It’s all about getting the best out of both worlds –&nbsp;we ask TomTom’ers to come to the office two days a week, and the remaining three are free to be worked in either location.Improve your home office with a setup budget and get extra support with a monthly allowance.&nbsp;Enjoy options to work from your home country and abroad for a set number of days each year, to visit family and friends, or to simply explore the world we’re mapping. &nbsp;Take the holidays you want with a competitive holiday plan, plus an extra day off to celebrate your birthday.&nbsp;Join annual events like our      Hackathon and DevDays to bring your ideas to life with talented teammates from around the world.&nbsp;Become a part of our inclusive global culture and have the chance to collaborate with a diverse community – we have over 80 nationalities at TomTom!&nbsp;Find out more about&nbsp;our global benefits and enjoy additional local benefits tailored to your location.&nbsp;Meet your teamWe’re the User Experience Design team. Fueled by user insights and data analytics, our mission is to create powerful, easy-to-use products that delight our customers, from millions of drivers to automotive customers who embed our technologies in their vehicles. We deliver the design specifications for all TomTom’s products. Joining us, you'll be part of a team that brings together design disciplines from user research to interaction, concept and visual design. Together, we'll continue to develop a map that people trust all around the world.  At TomTom...You’ll help people find their way in the world. In 2004, TomTom revolutionized how the world moves with the introduction of the first portable navigation device. Now, we intend to do it again by engineering the first-ever real-time map, the smartest and most useful map on the planet.Work with a team of 3,600+ unique, curious and passionate problem-solvers. Together, we’ll open up a world of possibilities for car manufacturers, enterprises and developers to help people understand and get closer to the world around them.After you applyOur recruitment team will work hard to give you a meaningful experience throughout your journey with us, no matter the outcome. Your application will be screened closely and you can rest assured that all follow-up actions will be thorough, from assessments and interviews all the way through onboarding. To find out more about our application process, check out our hiring FAQs.TomTom is an equal opportunity employerTomTom is where you can find your place in the world. Every day we welcome, nurture and celebrate differences. Why? Because your uniqueness is what makes you, you. No matter your culture or background, you’ll find your impact at TomTom.&nbsp;Research also shows that sometimes women and underrepresented communities can be hesitant to apply for positions unless they believe they meet 100% of the criteria. If you can relate to this, please know that we’d love to hear from you.Find more English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands on Arbeitnow

We are building a high-performance ADAS Online team focused on advancing state-of-the-art machine learning and AI algorithms for scene understanding and environmental awareness.As a machine learning applied scientist, you will contribute to the development and improvement of models within the in-vehicle spatial awareness stack. Work hands-on across data, experimentation, and evaluation pipelines, and grow your ability to tackle increasingly complex engineering challenges in a fast-moving team.This spatial awareness stack will leverage modern transformer and end-to-end architectures to transform vehicle sensor data along with real-time 3D map data from the cloud into a 3D, semantically defined environment identifying all static and dynamic objects.&nbsp;What You’ll Do

Develop a solid understanding of the team's physical AI roadmap and contribute ideas that improve algorithms within your area of ownership;
Implement and improve ML / vision transformer models for 3D awareness;
Produce instance detections and segmentation masks, instance tracking, and occupancy modelling;
Contribute to multi-modal fusion pipelines (camera, LiDAR, RADAR), building and validating components against defined requirements;
Apply Transformer-based and representation learning techniques within established frameworks, building confidence in large-scale model development;
Run experiments and benchmarks with guidance, producing clear results and contributing to the team's evaluation practices;
Participate in translating research into production, learning what makes ML solutions reliable and scalable;
Actively seek feedback from senior engineers and apply it to continuously improve the quality of your work.

What You'll Need

3+ years of experience in machine learning, vision transformers, diffusion, or computer vision;
Expertise in modern deep learning architectures;
Hands-on experience with PyTorch (or equivalent frameworks);
Understanding of what is needed to build and deploy large-scale ML models;
Strong ownership and bias toward execution;
Data-driven mindset with rigorous evaluation practices;
Ability to operate effectively in fast-paced environments;
Clear communication of technical trade-offs;
High standards for code quality and reproducibility;
Comfortable navigating ambiguity in complex technical domains.

Nice to Have 

Experience in autonomous systems or robotics perception;
Publications or patents in machine learning or perception;
Experience with 3D data representations (meshes, point clouds, BEV, voxel grids).

What we offer A competitive compensation package, of course. &nbsp;Time and resources to grow and develop, including a personal development budget and paid leave for learning days, as well as paid access to e-learning resources such as O’Reilly and LinkedIn Learning.&nbsp;Time to support life outside of work, with enhanced parental leave plus paid leave to care for loved ones and volunteer in local communities.&nbsp;&nbsp;Work flexibility, where TomTom’ers, in agreement with their manager and team, use both the office and home to focus, collaborate, learn and socialize. It’s all about getting the best out of both worlds –&nbsp;we ask TomTom’ers to come to the office two days a week, and the remaining three are free to be worked in either location.Improve your home office with a setup budget and get extra support with a monthly allowance.&nbsp;Enjoy options to work from your home country and abroad for a set number of days each year, to visit family and friends, or to simply explore the world we’re mapping. &nbsp;Take the holidays you want with a competitive holiday plan, plus an extra day off to celebrate your birthday.&nbsp;Join annual events like our      Hackathon and DevDays to bring your ideas to life with talented teammates from around the world.&nbsp;Become a part of our inclusive global culture and have the chance to collaborate with a diverse community – we have over 80 nationalities at TomTom!&nbsp;Find out more about&nbsp;our global benefits and enjoy additional local benefits tailored to your location.&nbsp;Meet your teamWe are the ADAS &amp; ADS Product Unit, leading the production of TomTom’s HD maps and ADAS technology.&nbsp;&nbsp;In a diverse team of applied scientists, engineers, data scientists, and more, equipped with a broad array of expertise, you’ll collaborate on groundbreaking location-based technologies and applications. &nbsp;More specifically, you’ll be at the forefront of the creation of advanced HD maps. You’ll also help update these in real-time, ensuring our maps are pushing the world forward instantly. These maps will then go on to empower the largest car manufacturers, transportation giants, and major tech companies around the world. At TomTom...You’ll help people find their way in the world. In 2004, TomTom revolutionized how the world moves with the introduction of the first portable navigation device. Now, we intend to do it again by engineering the first-ever real-time map, the smartest and most useful map on the planet.Work with a team of  3,300+ unique, curious and passionate problem-solvers. Together, we’ll open up a world of possibilities for car manufacturers, enterprises and developers to help people understand and get closer to the world around them.After you applyOur recruitment team will work hard to give you a meaningful experience throughout your journey with us, no matter the outcome. Your application will be screened closely and you can rest assured that all follow-up actions will be thorough, from assessments and interviews all the way through onboarding. To find out more about our application process, check out our hiring FAQs.TomTom is an equal opportunity employerTomTom is where you can find your place in the world. Every day we welcome, nurture and celebrate differences. Why? Because your uniqueness is what makes you, you. No matter your culture or background, you’ll find your impact at TomTom.&nbsp;Research also shows that sometimes women and underrepresented communities can be hesitant to apply for positions unless they believe they meet 100% of the criteria. If you can relate to this, please know that we’d love to hear from you.Find more English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands on Arbeitnow

About the role&nbsp;We are looking for a hands-on Endpoint Automation Engineer to design, build and continuously improve the automation that powers our global endpoint environment. This is a cross-platform engineering role focused on making endpoint services scalable, secure, reliable and consistent across Windows, macOS, Linux and mobile devices.&nbsp;&nbsp;You will replace repetitive administration with reusable code, integrations and event-driven workflows. Working across endpoint management, identity, security, application delivery, observability and device lifecycle services, you will use the Microsoft technology stack as core platforms while creating automation that operates across a broader endpoint technology ecosystem.&nbsp;


Engineering mindset&nbsp;Automation is the product, not an afterthought. We are looking for someone who sees a repetitive task, fragile hand-off or one-off script and asks, “How can we make this reliable, reusable and self-service?”&nbsp;&nbsp;You should be comfortable investigating unfamiliar systems, working from API documentation and turning operational requirements into maintainable automation. Your designs account for failure, test before release, instrument what you build and favour reusable services over isolated scripts. You take ownership from design through operation, document your solutions and balance long-term engineering improvements with immediate business needs.&nbsp;&nbsp;What success looks like&nbsp;You will measurably reduce manual work, deployment lead time and configuration inconsistency across the endpoint estate. Provisioning, configuration, software delivery, patching, compliance and lifecycle processes will become increasingly automated, observable, auditable and recoverable.&nbsp;&nbsp;Over time, you will help establish a shared Endpoint Automation model in which cross-platform services are delivered through reusable code, APIs, pipelines and common engineering standards rather than only platform-specific administration.&nbsp;

What you'll do


Endpoint Platforms &amp; Automation&nbsp;




Design and maintain automation frameworks for endpoint enrollment, provisioning, configuration, application delivery and retirement.&nbsp;






Build reusable tools, services and workflows using PowerShell, APIs and other appropriate programming languages.&nbsp;






Integrate endpoint platforms with identity, security, infrastructure, asset and service-management systems.&nbsp;






Apply Git, CI/CD, automated testing and configuration-as-code practices to make endpoint changes controlled, repeatable and auditable.&nbsp;






Identify manual, error-prone or fragmented processes and redesign them as resilient, self-service automation.&nbsp;




Security, Compliance &amp; Observability&nbsp;




Translate endpoint security and compliance requirements into policy-as-code, automated controls and measurable outcomes.&nbsp;






Automate operating-system and third-party application patching, vulnerability remediation and exception handling.&nbsp;






Build automated guardrails for encryption, endpoint protection, authentication and device compliance.&nbsp;






Create telemetry, dashboards and alerting that provide actionable visibility into automation performance, device health and risk.&nbsp;






Partner with Security teams to automate evidence collection, audit reporting and remediation workflows.&nbsp;




Engineering, Lifecycle &amp; Support&nbsp;




Define endpoint automation architecture, engineering standards and a roadmap that reduces operational effort and platform fragmentation.&nbsp;






Engineer automated application packaging, deployment, update and rollback pipelines.&nbsp;








Evaluate platform capabilities, APIs and emerging technologies for opportunities to simplify or extend endpoint automation.&nbsp;






Troubleshoot complex failures across automation, endpoints, identity, networking, security and device-management services.&nbsp;






Convert recurring incidents and support escalations into automated detection, remediation or prevention.&nbsp;






Document automation designs, operating models and support procedures, and enable teams to use them effectively.&nbsp;




What you'll need&nbsp;


Minimum 5 years of experience building automation for endpoint operations in a modern enterprise environment.&nbsp;





Hands-on expertise with Microsoft Intune, Entra ID, Windows Autopilot and endpoint compliance, with the ability to automate their administration through supported interfaces.&nbsp;






Demonstrated ability to create production-quality automation using PowerShell, REST APIs, Microsoft Graph, or other programming languages.&nbsp;






Experience automating application packaging, deployment, patching and vulnerability-remediation workflows.&nbsp;






Practical knowledge of Git, CI/CD, testing, secrets management and controlled configuration deployment.&nbsp;






Strong understanding of endpoint security, modern identity and the interaction between devices, cloud services and automation platforms.&nbsp;






A bachelor’s degree in IT, Computer Science or equivalent practical experience.&nbsp;




Additional experience that would be valuable:&nbsp;




Automating macOS and Jamf, Linux endpoint management, or mobile device-management platforms.&nbsp;






Azure or other cloud services for hosting functions, workflows, integrations and automation data.&nbsp;






Infrastructure or configuration as code, automated testing and release pipelines.&nbsp;






Vulnerability-management, endpoint-security or observability platforms with accessible APIs.&nbsp;






SSO, OAuth, SQL and data-analysis technologies used in system integrations and reporting.&nbsp;


What we offer A competitive compensation package, of course. &nbsp;Time and resources to grow and develop, including a personal development budget and paid leave for learning days, as well as paid access to e-learning resources such as O’Reilly and LinkedIn Learning.&nbsp;Time to support life outside of work, with enhanced parental leave plus paid leave to care for loved ones and volunteer in local communities.&nbsp;&nbsp;Work flexibility, where TomTom’ers, in agreement with their manager and team, use both the office and home to focus, collaborate, learn and socialize. It’s all about getting the best out of both worlds –&nbsp;we ask TomTom’ers to come to the office two days a week, and the remaining three are free to be worked in either location.Improve your home office with a setup budget and get extra support with a monthly allowance.&nbsp;Enjoy options to work from your home country and abroad for a set number of days each year, to visit family and friends, or to simply explore the world we’re mapping. &nbsp;Take the holidays you want with a competitive holiday plan, plus an extra day off to celebrate your birthday.&nbsp;Join annual events like our      Hackathon and DevDays to bring your ideas to life with talented teammates from around the world.&nbsp;Become a part of our inclusive global culture and have the chance to collaborate with a diverse community – we have over 80 nationalities at TomTom!&nbsp;Find out more about&nbsp;our global benefits and enjoy additional local benefits tailored to your location.&nbsp;Meet your teamWe’re Employee IT. We’re on a mission to deliver a seamless user experience for TomTom'ers across. Whether we're creating solutions to enable collaboration, increase productivity or help people communicate, your work will ensure TomTom'ers are equipped to create the first real-time map. In our team, you’ll help design, develop, deliver, operate and support solutions through a defined set of services, so that we can continue to bring people closer to the world around them. At TomTom...You’ll help people find their way in the world. In 2004, TomTom revolutionized how the world moves with the introduction of the first portable navigation device. Now, we intend to do it again by engineering the first-ever real-time map, the smartest and most useful map on the planet.Work with a team of 3,300+ unique, curious and passionate problem-solvers. Together, we’ll open up a world of possibilities for car manufacturers, enterprises and developers to help people understand and get closer to the world around them.After you applyOur recruitment team will work hard to give you a meaningful experience throughout your journey with us, no matter the outcome. Your application will be screened closely and you can rest assured that all follow-up actions will be thorough, from assessments and interviews all the way through onboarding. To find out more about our application process, check out our hiring FAQs.TomTom is an equal opportunity employerTomTom is where you can find your place in the world. Every day we welcome, nurture and celebrate differences. Why? Because your uniqueness is what makes you, you. No matter your culture or background, you’ll find your impact at TomTom.&nbsp;Research also shows that sometimes women and underrepresented communities can be hesitant to apply for positions unless they believe they meet 100% of the criteria. If you can relate to this, please know that we’d love to hear from you.Find Jobs in Netherlands on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Mavericks Wanted&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;When was the last time you achieved the impossible? If that thought feels overwhelming, you might want to pause here, but if it sparks excitement...read on&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;In 2015, we pioneered a “moneyball for biotech” approach, pooling projects and promising early-stage research from academia together under one financial umbrella to reduce risk and unleash innovation. This model allows science and small teams of experts to lead the way. We build bridges to groundbreaking advancements in rare&amp;nbsp;disease, and&amp;nbsp;develop life-changing medicines for patients with unmet needs as fast as humanly possible. &lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Together we define white space, push boundaries, and empower people to solve problems. If you&#39;re someone who defies convention, join us and work alongside some of the most respected minds in the industry. Together, we&#39;ll&amp;nbsp;ask&amp;nbsp;&quot;why not?&quot; and help reengineer the future of biopharma. At BridgeBio, we value curiosity and experimentation—including the ethical &amp;amp; thoughtful use of AI to improve clarity, speed, and quality of work.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;About BridgeBio Pharma, Inc.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;BridgeBio&amp;nbsp;is a biopharmaceutical company dedicated to discovering, developing, and delivering transformative medicines for patients living with genetic diseases and genetically defined cancers. Since our founding in 2015, we have built a diverse portfolio of more than 20 drug development programs, ranging from early discovery to late-stage clinical trials, across multiple therapeutic areas including precision oncology, cardiology, endocrinology, neurology, and renal disease. We have already achieved regulatory approval for three therapies and continue to advance promising science from academia into meaningful treatments for patients worldwide.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Who We Are&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;BridgeBio is a global biotechnology company with our Global Headquarters located in San Francisco, USA, and our International HQ located in Zug, Switzerland. Since establishing our European presence in 2021, we’ve been building empowered, high-performing teams across countries — experienced colleagues who move quickly, take ownership, and are fueling the company’s international growth.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;At BridgeBio, you’ll find an energetic and collaborative culture where pragmatism meets bold decision-making. We embrace uncertainty with confidence, guided by our commitment to making a meaningful impact for patients. Our people are trusted and empowered, united by urgency, purpose, and the drive to advance science for patients around the world.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Manager, Commercial Sourcing and Contracts will report directly to the Head of International Supply Chain. This role will be responsible for supporting the development and execution of sourcing strategies, managing the end-to-end contracting lifecycle for commercial goods and services. You will partner closely with cross-functional stakeholders (Supply Chain, Legal, Finance, CMC and Quality) to manage supplier relationships and ensure contractual compliance across Contract Manufacturing Organizations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sourcing Strategy &amp;amp; Execution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the development and implementation of sourcing strategies for Contract Manufacturing Organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support RFP processes, supplier evaluations, and negotiations to secure optimal cost, quality, and service outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct market analysis and benchmarking to support the identification of sourcing opportunities and mitigate supply risk&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive supplier consolidation, dual-sourcing, or diversification strategies where appropriate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contract Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft, negotiate, and finalize commercial contracts, master service agreements (MSAs), and supply agreements in collaboration with the relevant stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a contract repository/tracker ensuring visibility of key terms, renewal dates, and obligations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage contract amendments, renewals, and terminations in line with business needs and risk exposure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Supplier Relationship Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as primary Commercial Supply Chain point of contact for Contract Manufacturing Organizations, managing performance reviews and escalations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor supplier performance against SLAs/KPIs and drive corrective action plans where needed with relevant stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support supplier risk assessments (financial, operational, compliance) in coordination with Quality and Supply Chain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Where You’ll Work&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hybrid role based in the Netherlands, with approximately 10–15% travel anticipated to visit Contract Manufacturing Organizations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Who You Are&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in a related field, such as Supply Chain, Logistics, or Business Administration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 10 years of supply chain experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life sciences industry experience; experience with commercial products is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience negotiating and managing commercial contracts with Contract Manufacturing Organizations in a regulated environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong negotiation skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to build and sustain trusted relationships, both internally and externally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent stakeholder management and cross-functional collaboration skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical mindset with the ability to translate contract terms into sourcing decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detail-oriented, organized, and comfortable managing multiple contracts/projects simultaneously&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in English, both written and spoken&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Rewarding Those Who Make the Mission Possible&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have high expectations for our team members. We make sure those working hard for patients are rewarded and cared for in return.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Market-leading compensation&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid work model – we value your flexibility in how you work, but encourage time in the office to strengthen our culture, collaboration, and sense of community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Career development through regular feedback, continuous education, and professional development programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recognition for strong performance through financial rewards, peer-to-peer feedback, and growth opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As a global company, our comprehensive benefits may vary based on location.&amp;nbsp; &lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;We have high expectations for our team members. We make sure those working hard for patients are rewarded and cared for in return.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
