&lt;h3 class=&quot;markdown__heading&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your IMC Journey as a Graduate Hardware Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Graduate Hardware Engineer at IMC, you’ll begin your career with a comprehensive five-week Global Trainee Programme led by our experienced engineers and traders, together with fellow graduates from our offices in Europe, the United States, and Asia-Pacific.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;After completing the programme, you’ll continue your professional development in your&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;local office, working closely with your mentor, an experienced IMC engineer, to apply what you’ve learned to real-world, high-impact projects.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your work will go far beyond coding, you’ll gain a deep understanding of IMC’s field-programmable gate array RTL/FPGA development process, learn how technology drives our unique trading strategies, and collaborate with some of the brightest minds in both engineering and trading.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;markdown__heading&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Core Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, implement, and validate improvements to IMC’s FPGA trading systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work hands-on with cutting-edge hardware and development tools to optimise system performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in pair programming sessions, peer code reviews, and design discussions to ensure high-quality solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with traders and software engineers to deliver robust, low-latency systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continue to grow through workshops, training sessions, and networking events with engineers across all IMC regions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;markdown__heading&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Skills and Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recently graduated (or graduating by 2027) with a degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or a related discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with a hardware descriptive language such as VHDL, Verilog, or SystemVerilog&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in at least one programming language (C++ or Python preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving abilities with a passion for tackling complex technical challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative mindset; you thrive in environments that value&amp;nbsp;creativity, innovation, and teamwork&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuine interest in how technology shapes financial markets (no prior finance experience required)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Available to start full-time in February or August 2027&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
